00:05:19.135 --> 00:05:24.153
and it was later taken down. The Starfall disc is today's engineering deep dive,

00:05:24.153 --> 00:05:29.873
Because that flat shape is doing three jobs at once that a classic cone would split among different parts.

00:05:30.413 --> 00:05:36.753
In 1953, H. Julian Allen and AJ Eggers showed that a blunt body stays cooler than a sharp one.

00:05:37.393 --> 00:05:42.553
The shock stands off from the wall, and most of the kinetic energy stays in the air, not in the metal.

00:05:43.153 --> 00:05:47.253
Reentry from low-earth orbit hits about 7.8 kilometers per second.

00:05:47.833 --> 00:05:51.153
A back-of-envelope 30 megajoules in every kilogram of vehicle.

00:05:51.153 --> 00:05:56.013
Only a few percent of that energy reaches the shield as heat flux. Peak heating

00:05:56.013 --> 00:06:01.793
still lands at the stagnation point, where flow comes to a dead stop at roughly 1-3 megawatts

00:06:01.793 --> 00:06:07.673
per square meter on a typical capsule, a textbook range, not a company spec. Heat flux scales

00:06:07.673 --> 00:06:13.053
with velocity cubed and falls as the square root of effective nose radius, so a wider face

00:06:13.053 --> 00:06:18.433
is a cooler face per square meter. A low, wide disc behaves like a very large nose radius.

00:06:18.433 --> 00:06:23.913
Double that radius and peak flux drops about 30%. Spread the load over roughly

00:06:23.913 --> 00:06:28.993
seven and a half square meters of windward phase, a back of envelope area for this geometry,

00:06:29.493 --> 00:06:34.933
and each tile sees less. A flat windward phase also lets you lay silica tiles in a simple

00:06:34.933 --> 00:06:40.633
grid instead of compounding curves around a cone, which cuts unique tooling. Wave a magic

00:06:40.633 --> 00:06:46.413
wand and the raw aluminum plus silica tile feedstock is a few tens of dollars per kilogram of structure.

00:06:46.413 --> 00:06:52.433
After finished aerospace hardware often lands 20-50 times that, an idiot index finished

00:06:52.433 --> 00:06:57.613
cost over raw inputs because one shot thermal protection and one off molds dominate.

00:06:58.293 --> 00:07:04.033
Aluminum melts near 660 degrees Celsius and silica tiles keep the structure under that with

00:07:04.033 --> 00:07:06.773
only a few centimeters of low conductivity ceramic.

00:07:07.373 --> 00:07:12.553
